# The Endministrator for the challenge "20 Arts Infliction → Final DMG Dealt +50 %".
#
# Built for one account: roster/endfield.profile.yaml, snapshot of 2026-09-25.
# Gear and weapons were picked for this challenge (worked out that day):
#
#   Endmin   sk.12/12/12/12  Grand Vision r1 (6,6,3)      Grizzled Edge ×3 +3, P3
#   Estella  sk.9/9/10/9     OBJ Razorhorn r5 (3,3,3)     Type 50 Yinglung ×3, P5
#   Alesh    sk.9/10/12/10   Never Rest (4,4,3)           AIC Fieldwork ×4 (UGE), P5
#   Antal    sk.6/6/6/6      Stanza of Memorials (4,4,2)  AIC Fieldwork ×3 + Frontiers Suit, P5
#
# Stanza is borrowed from Perlica, Never Rest was free. Give Stanza back afterwards.
#
# The challenge counter counts PER ENEMY (checked in a fight with Rossi's
# ultimate), so area applications pay off many times over.
#
# The AXIS is Cryo. Heat and Electric stay out: on top of Cryo they cause a
# different reaction and eat the stacks before Alesh's battle skill.
#
# Who applies Arts Infliction:
#   Estella BS  — Cryo to everyone on the line of the strike  (+1 per enemy)
#   Antal CS    — one more stack of the same infliction on the Focus target (+1, one target)
#   Alesh ULT   — Cryo over a large area                       (+1 per enemy)
# Nobody else. Alesh's battle skill CONSUMES the stacks, it does not apply them.
#
# The chain sustains itself, the combos arm each other:
#   Estella BS → Cryo → Antal CS (+1 stack) → Alesh BS (eats it, Solidification)
#   → Estella CS (Lift breaks the freeze: Shatter, physical damage)
#   → Alesh CS (Arts Reaction consumed) → Endmin CS (crystals)
#   → Endmin BS (Crush breaks the crystals, P1: 50 SP back).

title: Endmin cryo: Endmin / Estella / Alesh / Antal
team: Endministrator, Estella, Alesh, Antal

# ===========================================================================
variant: basic
# ===========================================================================

Antal: BS
# Focus on the main target: lasts 60 s, one target on the field. Antal's
# combo works only on it, so mark whoever will live the longest.
# His Electric/Heat Susceptibility is useless here — the price of the duplicator.

Estella: BS
# Cryo along the line. Line the enemies up: each one hit is +1 to the counter.

Antal: CS
# Trigger: the Focus target received Arts Infliction. A second Cryo stack.
# This combo deals damage and also arms the Endministrator's combo — but the
# Endministrator is NOT pressed here: Estella's Lift would break the crystals,
# and P1 (50 SP) would be lost.

Alesh: BS
# Eats both stacks → Solidification at Status Level II on the Focus target
# (SL I on the rest). SP Recovery: 25 for 2 stacks (lv 10) + 10 from P1.
# Every SP recovery is a Never Rest stack: Physical DMG +4 % to the others
# for 30 s, up to 5 stacks. Alesh recovers SP with his battle skill, combo and
# ultimate, so the +20 % holds almost all the time.

Estella: CS
# Trigger: Solidification. Lift breaks the freeze → Shatter, physical.
# Physical Susceptibility 15 % (combo lv 10) — on all of the team's physical
# damage, and the Endministrator hits inside this window. Talent E2: her next
# battle skill returns 15 SP.

Alesh: CS
# Trigger: Arts Reaction consumed. +15 SP (lv 12), a chance of Rare Fin
# (+10 SP, and P3 gives the team ATK +15 % for 10 s).

Endministrator: CS
# Trigger: a teammate's combo. Crystals on the target, a seal for 5 s.
# Grand Vision: applying crystals → the Endministrator's next battle skill or
# ultimate gets Physical DMG +57.6 %. Alesh's Solidification does NOT arm
# this effect: the condition is "when the wielder applies".

Endministrator: BS
# Crush breaks the crystals: P1 returns 50 SP, talent E2 gives ATK +30 %,
# P2 gives half of that to the others.

Alesh: CS~ [crystals consumed — a second trigger, if the 8 s cooldown is back]

Endministrator: BA > FS

# ===========================================================================
variant: wave
# A pack of small enemies. Open with Alesh's ultimate, so the counter goes
# up on all of them at once.
# ===========================================================================

Antal: BS
Alesh: ULT
# Cryo to everyone in a large area: +1 to the counter for each. Returns SP
# for kills (up to 100).

Estella: BS
# A second Cryo stack on everyone in the line (+Arts Burst): another +1 each.

Antal: CS
# A third stack on the Focus target.

Alesh: BS
# Solidification SL III on the Focus target, SL II on those hit by both.

Estella: CS
Alesh: CS

Antal: ULT~
# The ultimate itself (Electric/Heat Amp) is useless here — it is pressed for
# Stanza of Memorials: the other three are of another element and get ATK
# +11.2 % for 20 s. Put it right before the Endministrator's burst, so the
# window covers her ultimate and battle skill.

Endministrator: CS
Endministrator: ULT~ [hits the crystals: extra hit 600 %, P3 +15 energy; the Grand Vision buff goes here]
Endministrator: BS

# ===========================================================================
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT CHECK
#
# The trigger logic is validated, not the timing or the resources.
#
# The counter per "basic" cycle: 2 applications on the Focus target + 1 for
# each extra enemy on Estella's line. On a single target that is 10 cycles —
# the challenge has to be done on packs, not on a boss.
#
# SP (roughly, a cycle is ~25 s, set by Antal's combo cooldown): 4 battle
# skills = 400; back come Alesh 35 + 15, Endmin 50, Estella 15, regen ≈ 200.
# The first cycle is ~85 short; from the second one Antal skips his battle
# skill (Focus lasts 60 s) — and the cycle comes out positive. Final Strikes
# cover the rest.
#
# The Endministrator's refund is an SP Return: spending it gives no Ultimate Energy.
# ===========================================================================
